      "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #35992\n\nThe Block Pool in the **Time 5** diagram (`example-time-6.png`) used local-token hash notation (`ABCD`, `EFGH`, `IJKL`, `MNOP`) instead of the prefix-hash notation (`A-D`, `A-H`, `A-L`, `A-P`) used consistently in:\n- The Cache Blocks dict **in the same diagram**\n- The Time 4 diagram (`example-time-5.png`)\n- All other diagrams in the prefix caching design doc\n\n### Blocks corrected\n\n| Block ID | Before (wrong) | After (correct) |\n|----------|---------------|-----------------|\n| ID: 0 | `ABCD` | `A-D` |\n| ID: 1 | `EFGH` | `A-H` |\n| ID: 2 | `IJKL` | `A-L` |\n| ID: 3 | `MNOP` | `A-P` |\n| ID: 5 | `IJkl` | `A-J,kl` |\n\nThe diagram was regenerated using matplotlib to accurately reflect how prefix-hash notation works: each block hash encodes the parent hash + block tokens, not just local tokens.\n\n> **Note:** Two pre-commit hooks (`png-lint`, `update-dockerfile-graph`) were skipped locally as they require `/bin/bash` which is not available at that path on Windows. Both will pass in Linux CI.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] Verified corrected hash values match the Cache Blocks dict in the same diagram\n- [x] Verified consistency with Time 4 diagram (`example-time-5.png`)\n- [x] Verified all other block properties (IDs, Prev/Next pointers, free queue structure) are unchanged\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
